│
└── .venv/
Step 5. Start our first AI control server
Inside backend, create a file named main.py.

Paste this code:


from fastapi import FastAPI
from datetime import datetime

app = FastAPI(title="Puneet AI TV")

@app.get("/")
def home():
    return {
        "project": "Puneet AI TV",
        "status": "running",
        "message": "Your AI TV system is ready for development"
    }

@app.get("/health")
def health():
    return {
        "status": "healthy",
        "time": datetime.now().isoformat()
    }

@app.get("/devices")
def devices():
    return {
        "tv": "not_connected",
        "dish_receiver": "not_connected",
        "whatsapp": "not_connected"
    }


Run it from the main project directory:

uvicorn backend.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000

Open this address in your laptop browser:

Open Puneet AI TV server
You should see a JSON response confirming that the server is running.

You can also open:

Open API dashboard
First milestone Local AI control server running.

6. How our final controls will work
One technical clarification before we build further:

OnePlus TV: We will test network control and ADB compatibility.

DD Free Dish: We will first investigate whether HDMI-CEC works. If not, an IR blaster may be needed to control channels and buttons.

WhatsApp: We will choose a reliable official integration for receiving commands and sending confirmations.

Voice: We can initially use your laptop microphone, then add TV-side voice support.

We won't uninstall system apps, change firmware or execute destructive commands without your approval.

